WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.640
Part three: a firm's history. Every client's past returns - the department's own JSON files - come into SimplyFile in a minute each. Here are ten returns from the last three years.

2
00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:28.550
Shree Ganesh Agarwal HUF's return for 2025-26. SimplyFile reads the form, the year and every figure, and finds the client with the same PAN.

3
00:00:29.155 --> 00:00:42.885
Kiran Kumar Rao's returns for 2023-24 and 2024-25 go in the same way. With this year's return, the firm now sees three years of his income.

4
00:00:51.686 --> 00:01:00.396
Sri Venkateswara Traders' ITR-5 for 2025-26 - a firm's return reads just as well.

5
00:01:02.561 --> 00:01:17.991
Lakshmi Narayana Textiles is not yet a client. Create the client straight from the return, start this year for them too - and download next year's statement with last year's figures beside every line, ready to fill.

6
00:01:18.608 --> 00:01:28.928
Ravi Teja filed with the firm for 2023-24 and not since. Import the return, and leave this year unstarted.

7
00:01:30.155 --> 00:01:43.935
Sunita Rao's original return for 2025-26, and then her revised return. The revised one takes the place of the original, which stays in the history as superseded.

8
00:01:52.702 --> 00:02:04.992
Mohammed Irfan's 2024-25 return was filed in November 2024 - the return itself says it was belated, and SimplyFile records it so.

9
00:02:05.594 --> 00:02:13.704
Deepa Krishnan lives in Singapore. Her return says non-resident, so her client record does too.

10
00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:22.790
Importing the Agarwal return a second time is refused - nothing is recorded twice.

11
00:02:27.765 --> 00:02:38.615
And a return can never land on the wrong client: Mohammed Irfan's return, pointed at the Agarwal HUF, is refused because the PAN does not match.

12
00:02:39.219 --> 00:02:47.859
Back in Firm analytics, the firm's whole history is in one place: returns on record across four assessment years.

13
00:02:48.469 --> 00:02:54.589
Year on year: clients, returns filed and income handled for each assessment year.

14
00:02:55.202 --> 00:03:10.392
And new opportunities from the history: growing clients - income up by a quarter or more - who are ready for more services; shrinking clients to check in with early; and lapsed clients who filed with the firm before and could be called back.

15
00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:21.699
SimplyFile - from a client's past returns and this year's Excel to the department's JSON, with the whole practice in view. Thank you for watching.
